1
00:00:00,624 --> 00:00:06,592
Billions in insurance and banking still run on COBOL. Rewriting it is easy. Proving

2
00:00:06,592 --> 00:00:12,560
the rewrite behaves exactly the same is the hard part. This is COBOL Phoenix.

3
00:00:13,520 --> 00:00:22,669
We import an insurance rating system. It is parsed deterministically, with no AI guessing: three programs, three copybooks, twenty

4
00:00:22,669 --> 00:00:31,819
seven business rules, and three file input output statements we do not translate, each reported with its exact line.

5
00:00:32,719 --> 00:00:38,839
Every dependency points to real source. Here is the base premium rule: its

6
00:00:38,839 --> 00:00:44,958
inputs, its outputs, and the compute rounded statement, cited to the original lines.

7
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:52,273
One click generates a FastAPI service, with decimal arithmetic and schemas derived from the

8
00:00:52,273 --> 00:00:58,688
COBOL picture clauses. Every Python statement maps back to the COBOL line it came from.

9
00:00:59,590 --> 00:01:13,656
Now the proof. The original program runs in a sandboxed GnuCOBOL container with no network, and the generated Python runs beside it. Fixtures, boundary values derived from the code, edge

10
00:01:13,656 --> 00:01:27,723
cases and random records. One hundred twenty seven of one hundred twenty seven cases are identical. Then mutation analysis tests the tests, and lists every injected fault they would miss.

11
00:01:28,623 --> 00:01:35,276
Does the verifier actually catch mistakes? We inject one tiny fault: a missing rounded.

12
00:01:35,276 --> 00:01:41,930
Eight cases fail, down to the cent, with the exact field and its copybook line.

13
00:01:42,831 --> 00:01:51,557
And it is not just our sample. On an independent public insurance repository, the generated underwriting service matches GnuCOBOL

14
00:01:51,557 --> 00:02:00,283
on one hundred eighty of one hundred eighty cases. Mutation analysis even exposed a business rule that can never fire.

15
00:02:01,184 --> 00:02:10,093
Evidence for every rule. Proof for every build. COBOL Phoenix. Preserve the logic, rebuild the future.
